1
00:00:01,969 --> 00:00:03,146
GORDON: <i>Previously on</i> Gotham...

2
00:00:03,170 --> 00:00:05,935
I have walked this
earth for centuries.

3
00:00:06,173 --> 00:00:09,507
Only you can kill me
and only with that dagger.

4
00:00:10,143 --> 00:00:11,702
(GROANS)

5
00:00:13,780 --> 00:00:16,807
- What did I say?
- I can help you get Tabitha back.

6
00:00:17,050 --> 00:00:19,576
Professor Hugo Strange is
the one man who can cure you.

7
00:00:19,853 --> 00:00:22,049
Join me, and we will find him.

8
00:00:22,489 --> 00:00:23,855
(GASPING)

9
00:00:24,358 --> 00:00:25,598
Okay. But you'd better deliver.

10
00:00:25,893 --> 00:00:27,225
Why would I help you?

11
00:00:27,694 --> 00:00:29,720
You love me. You've
loved me all along.

12
00:00:31,665 --> 00:00:34,692
What's your record for how many
banks you've robbed in one day?

13
00:00:34,801 --> 00:00:36,463
<i>You're playing a
dangerous game, Lee.</i>

14
00:00:37,504 --> 00:00:39,996
LELIA: <i>Ra's al Ghul chose
you to pass on his spirit.</i>

15
00:00:40,340 --> 00:00:42,241
<i>We have much more to show you.</i>

16
00:00:42,709 --> 00:00:46,510
BARBARA: <i>All my life, I have
known that I was meant for more.</i>

17
00:00:46,847 --> 00:00:47,906
<i>This isn't you.</i>

18
00:00:48,048 --> 00:00:50,415
I'm not gonna let your
jealousy distract me.

19
00:00:50,584 --> 00:00:54,214
Ladies, escort Ms.
Galavan to the street.

20
00:00:54,454 --> 00:00:57,083
MAN: <i>We serve the one and
only true master, Ra's al Ghul.</i>

21
00:00:57,257 --> 00:00:59,419
- But he's dead.
- Death is only an illusion.

22
00:01:09,770 --> 00:01:10,770
(SWISHES)

23
00:01:13,440 --> 00:01:14,499
(GRUNTING)

24
00:01:20,948 --> 00:01:22,109
(KNIVES SWISHING)

25
00:01:23,483 --> 00:01:24,542
(BARBARA PANTING)

26
00:01:25,819 --> 00:01:26,819
(SHOUTING) What the hell?

27
00:01:27,087 --> 00:01:29,716
- You didn't sense our approach?
- No, you're ninjas.

28
00:01:29,923 --> 00:01:31,551
The Demon's Head
gives its bearer power

29
00:01:31,625 --> 00:01:33,457
to see past, present,
future as one.

30
00:01:33,694 --> 00:01:35,287
You should have
anticipated our attack.

31
00:01:35,462 --> 00:01:36,521
So this was a test?

32
00:01:38,198 --> 00:01:39,689
I'm The Demon's Head.

33
00:01:39,766 --> 00:01:41,598
My hand is a
fricking light bulb.

34
00:01:41,702 --> 00:01:42,965
That is only its mark.

35
00:01:43,203 --> 00:01:45,263
You have yet to
access its real powers.

36
00:01:45,739 --> 00:01:47,435
You're questioning
whether I'm worthy?

37
00:01:48,141 --> 00:01:49,575
I'm sick of this.

38
00:01:50,077 --> 00:01:52,410
The men from the League,
Tabitha, and now you?

39
00:01:52,479 --> 00:01:53,674
You misunderstand.

40
00:01:54,147 --> 00:01:57,345
How do you think Ra's al Ghul became
the world's most fearsome warrior

41
00:01:57,451 --> 00:01:58,783
and ruled empires?

42
00:01:59,453 --> 00:02:01,285
He saw the future.

43
00:02:02,956 --> 00:02:04,288
So, attacking me was what,

44
00:02:04,891 --> 00:02:07,331
a way to jump-start it, like,
"Hey, Demon's Head, snap to it?"

45
00:02:07,594 --> 00:02:11,156
The powers of The Demon's Head
are triggered by intense emotions.

46
00:02:11,765 --> 00:02:14,792
All right. So next time,
don't go so easy on me.

47
00:02:16,236 --> 00:02:18,296
And take that
knife out of my face.

48
00:02:20,273 --> 00:02:22,139
(CAR ENGINE REVVING)

49
00:02:23,810 --> 00:02:25,438
(DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING)

50
00:02:36,957 --> 00:02:39,324
You don't have a covert
mode on this thing?

51
00:02:49,036 --> 00:02:50,299
(ENGINE REVVING STOPS)

52
00:02:56,410 --> 00:02:57,639
(SCOFFS)

53
00:02:57,711 --> 00:02:58,804
Show-off.

54
00:02:59,513 --> 00:03:01,491
So, you're gonna tell me
what Tabitha needs us for?

55
00:03:01,515 --> 00:03:05,646
All I know is it's about
Barbara, and it's important.

56
00:03:16,396 --> 00:03:18,365
- So, what's the emergency?
- Inside.

57
00:03:21,268 --> 00:03:22,268
You coming?

58
00:03:47,360 --> 00:03:48,692
Tabitha, what am I doing here?

59
00:03:48,995 --> 00:03:50,258
(SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING)

60
00:03:50,731 --> 00:03:51,731
(BRUCE GASPS)

61
00:03:51,832 --> 00:03:53,198
- What the heck?
- Wait.

62
00:03:53,266 --> 00:03:54,461
What the hell? What is this?

63
00:03:54,568 --> 00:03:56,079
I don't know. She
didn't tell me this part.

64
00:03:56,103 --> 00:03:58,732
Barbara needs our help.
She's gonna get herself killed.

65
00:03:58,805 --> 00:04:00,485
She has this thing
called The Demon's Head.

66
00:04:03,043 --> 00:04:05,354
- This is about Ra's al Ghul?
- He's the one who gave it to her.

67
00:04:05,378 --> 00:04:07,018
These guys are gonna
help us take it back.

68
00:04:07,047 --> 00:04:08,675
Okay, so why do you need Bruce?

69
00:04:17,057 --> 00:04:18,177
You're gonna bring him back.

70
00:04:20,193 --> 00:04:22,389
You can't do this.
Ra's wanted to die.

71
00:04:23,263 --> 00:04:24,322
He wanted me to kill him.

72
00:04:27,801 --> 00:04:29,326
And now we need him alive.

73
00:04:29,803 --> 00:04:31,669
No, no, no!

74
00:04:32,906 --> 00:04:33,930
(BRUCE STRAINING)

75
00:04:36,576 --> 00:04:38,943
No, no!

76
00:04:42,549 --> 00:04:46,316
Bone, flesh, breath. Come
back to us, our leader.

77
00:04:46,820 --> 00:04:48,550
Now we close the circle.

78
00:04:48,755 --> 00:04:50,555
We give you the blood
of the one who slew you.

79
00:04:54,094 --> 00:04:55,426
(TENSE MUSIC PLAYING)

80
00:05:01,268 --> 00:05:02,268
No.

81
00:05:03,370 --> 00:05:05,100
You have no idea
what you've done!

82
00:05:14,481 --> 00:05:16,006
(OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING)

83
00:05:32,465 --> 00:05:34,991
Five banks in one
night? You're joking.

84
00:05:35,335 --> 00:05:36,803
I wish. These guys were slick.

85
00:05:36,870 --> 00:05:38,948
Banks didn't even know
they were hit till they opened.

86
00:05:38,972 --> 00:05:41,117
One of the banks, the thieves
came in on boats through the sewer.

87
00:05:41,141 --> 00:05:42,261
Tunneled up into the vaults.

88
00:05:42,642 --> 00:05:45,373
All branches of Gotham Savings
and Loan. Why the same bank?

89
00:05:45,679 --> 00:05:48,274
Maybe a leak in
security, maybe a grudge.

90
00:05:48,448 --> 00:05:49,541
Five banks in one night.

91
00:05:50,050 --> 00:05:51,810
It's like someone was
trying to make a point.

92
00:05:52,152 --> 00:05:53,211
Prove how smart he is.

93
00:05:54,154 --> 00:05:55,816
- Ed Nygma?
- The bowler fits.

94
00:05:56,022 --> 00:05:57,320
Should I put out a BOLO on him?

95
00:05:57,724 --> 00:06:00,421
Sure. In the meantime, there's
someone else I can talk to.

96
00:06:00,894 --> 00:06:04,331
Say hey to Lee for me, won't
you? Tell her, nice shooting Sofia.

97
00:06:07,567 --> 00:06:08,899
What, I can't make a joke?

98
00:06:09,202 --> 00:06:10,202
That's what that was?

99
00:06:11,004 --> 00:06:12,666
Why don't you go
put that BOLO out?

100
00:06:17,644 --> 00:06:19,875
(PEOPLE CHATTERING INDISTINCTLY)

101
00:06:24,017 --> 00:06:25,485
- Here you go. No problem.
- Thanks.

102
00:06:25,986 --> 00:06:27,079
Look at them.

103
00:06:28,255 --> 00:06:29,450
We did good.

104
00:06:30,023 --> 00:06:31,047
Oh, yeah.

105
00:06:31,124 --> 00:06:33,525
My brilliance allowed us to
rob five banks in one night.

106
00:06:34,127 --> 00:06:35,595
Now these fine
folks of The Narrows

107
00:06:35,695 --> 00:06:37,907
are gonna be drowning in booze
and smokes for years to come.

108
00:06:37,931 --> 00:06:39,593
So inspiring.

109
00:06:39,699 --> 00:06:41,691
They're also gonna use
the money to buy food

110
00:06:42,102 --> 00:06:43,695
and clothing and medicine.

111
00:06:46,239 --> 00:06:47,239
What's wrong?

112
00:06:50,277 --> 00:06:51,540
What am I to you?

113
00:06:54,748 --> 00:06:56,740
A friend. A partner.

114
00:06:57,183 --> 00:06:59,084
Are you always this
amorous with your friends?

115
00:06:59,819 --> 00:07:01,197
I mean, I know that
only happened once.

116
00:07:01,221 --> 00:07:02,655
- Ed.
- Don't call me Ed.

117
00:07:03,423 --> 00:07:05,551
Hey, I care about you.

118
00:07:06,293 --> 00:07:07,625
I depend on you.

119
00:07:08,929 --> 00:07:10,295
You know what we've got planned.

120
00:07:11,097 --> 00:07:13,259
Other things are just
gonna have to wait.

121
00:07:14,067 --> 00:07:15,899
You're not stringing
me along, are you, Lee?

122
00:07:16,803 --> 00:07:18,135
Don't you wanna find out?

123
00:07:19,639 --> 00:07:20,902
The answer to the riddle?

124
00:07:25,078 --> 00:07:26,102
Maybe I do.

125
00:07:27,914 --> 00:07:29,154
Are we good for tomorrow night?

126
00:07:29,716 --> 00:07:31,582
Yeah. We just have
a few last details.

127
00:07:31,918 --> 00:07:35,252
And trust me, this is
gonna be a work of art.

128
00:07:35,922 --> 00:07:37,356
That sounds promising.

129
00:07:38,658 --> 00:07:41,287
Oh, what the hell, count us in.

130
00:07:50,236 --> 00:07:51,431
You could've told me.

131
00:07:51,738 --> 00:07:54,083
- You wouldn't have brought him.
- Yeah, because he's my friend.

132
00:07:54,107 --> 00:07:55,632
And what is Barbara? What am I?

133
00:07:56,443 --> 00:07:57,672
Pick a side and stick to it.

134
00:07:58,945 --> 00:08:01,608
RA'S AL GHUL: Do you
know what you've done?

135
00:08:02,315 --> 00:08:05,649
The years I spent
planning my death.

136
00:08:05,852 --> 00:08:08,651
- Now you've ruined it!
- Master.

137
00:08:09,856 --> 00:08:11,518
The woman you gave
The Demon's Head to,

138
00:08:11,858 --> 00:08:13,053
she started a war.

139
00:08:13,193 --> 00:08:15,992
I started that war!

140
00:08:16,129 --> 00:08:17,995
The League of Shadows was rotten

141
00:08:18,198 --> 00:08:21,168
and only through
violence could it be reborn.

142
00:08:25,538 --> 00:08:28,872
Master, our lives
are yours to take.

143
00:08:29,943 --> 00:08:32,970
But this woman does
not serve the League.

144
00:08:33,747 --> 00:08:36,376
Her goals are limited. Selfish.

145
00:08:36,716 --> 00:08:37,911
That's Barbara all right.

146
00:08:38,218 --> 00:08:40,244
Whatever faith you had
in her was misplaced.

147
00:08:40,553 --> 00:08:42,681
If she keeps The Demon's
Head, the League shall die.

148
00:08:43,890 --> 00:08:46,519
Wait, what do you mean, "if
she keeps The Demon's Head"?

149
00:08:47,327 --> 00:08:49,487
I thought you were supposed
to get it the second you...

150
00:08:49,896 --> 00:08:50,989
Came back.

151
00:08:51,264 --> 00:08:54,564
No. Barbara must give it to me.

152
00:08:57,170 --> 00:08:58,433
She'll never do that.

153
00:08:59,672 --> 00:09:03,200
Then I'll kill her and
rip it from her corpse.

154
00:09:05,211 --> 00:09:06,543
(SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING)

155
00:09:10,750 --> 00:09:12,048
PENGUIN: You owe us.

156
00:09:12,152 --> 00:09:13,381
(NYGMA LAUGHS)

157
00:09:13,853 --> 00:09:15,082
NYGMA: I'm sorry.

158
00:09:15,855 --> 00:09:16,855
We owe you how?

159
00:09:17,257 --> 00:09:19,817
Because we made you.

160
00:09:20,427 --> 00:09:24,660
Both of you. Without me, you
would still be trapped inside Ed.

161
00:09:25,565 --> 00:09:28,330
And you would still be
stitching up busted lips ringside.

162
00:09:29,002 --> 00:09:31,836
I need money to buy
back Sofia's capos.

163
00:09:32,705 --> 00:09:35,231
Butch is saving for
future medical expenses.

164
00:09:35,642 --> 00:09:36,642
(SCOFFS)

165
00:09:36,910 --> 00:09:39,436
What'd you make last
night? Three, four million?

166
00:09:40,647 --> 00:09:41,876
Say we go halfsies.

167
00:09:43,550 --> 00:09:44,711
I've heard your offer.

168
00:09:45,752 --> 00:09:48,312
And here's my counter. Bite me.

169
00:09:49,322 --> 00:09:51,223
I don't like people
coming into my club,

170
00:09:51,391 --> 00:09:53,826
telling me what to do.
And I don't like threats,

171
00:09:54,060 --> 00:09:55,494
implicit or otherwise,

172
00:09:55,595 --> 00:09:59,225
and I really don't like people
telling me they made me.

173
00:09:59,899 --> 00:10:00,992
NYGMA: Well said, Lee.

174
00:10:03,103 --> 00:10:04,162
(NYGMA CLAPPING)

175
00:10:04,504 --> 00:10:07,235
- Oh, God. Are you kidding me?
- What?

176
00:10:07,474 --> 00:10:08,737
Okay, we're done.

177
00:10:08,942 --> 00:10:11,776
I thought you got past all that
when you became the Riddler.

178
00:10:11,978 --> 00:10:12,978
Past what?

179
00:10:13,813 --> 00:10:15,611
Ed's pathetic adoration of her.

180
00:10:17,083 --> 00:10:19,575
But, no, clearly, he
passed it all into you,

181
00:10:20,153 --> 00:10:21,153
like a virus.

182
00:10:22,622 --> 00:10:24,318
She knows it and
she's using you.

183
00:10:25,158 --> 00:10:28,151
Shame on you, stringing
along this troubled man.

184
00:10:28,561 --> 00:10:30,325
- Get out!
- I don't think so.

185
00:10:32,298 --> 00:10:34,096
We did not come
here for violence.

186
00:10:35,335 --> 00:10:37,535
We came here hoping our
friends would honor their debts.

187
00:10:38,104 --> 00:10:39,766
Let us hope they
come to their senses.

188
00:10:42,642 --> 00:10:43,803
A little advice.

189
00:10:45,211 --> 00:10:48,648
Be sure to skim some off the
top when she tosses you aside.

190
00:10:56,956 --> 00:10:57,956
(DOOR OPENS)

191
00:10:58,691 --> 00:10:59,715
(DOOR CLOSES)

192
00:11:04,664 --> 00:11:06,064
(FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING)

193
00:11:08,601 --> 00:11:11,196
Kind of defeats the
purpose if I can hear you.

194
00:11:11,538 --> 00:11:13,370
Hello, Barbara.

195
00:11:16,709 --> 00:11:17,709
- Ra's.
- (GLASS BREAKING)

196
00:11:19,012 --> 00:11:20,173
Don't be afraid.

197
00:11:21,881 --> 00:11:24,851
(STUTTERING) What
happened? How are you even...

198
00:11:24,951 --> 00:11:26,146
It's a long story.

199
00:11:26,853 --> 00:11:27,853
But tell me,

200
00:11:28,555 --> 00:11:30,786
what have you done with my gift?

201
00:11:32,492 --> 00:11:34,017
Well, you might
have left a how-to.

202
00:11:35,361 --> 00:11:37,796
Plus, a heads-up to your
League of Shadows cronies.

203
00:11:38,164 --> 00:11:41,760
Turns out the old boys' club don't
appreciate a woman calling the shots.

204
00:11:42,035 --> 00:11:43,833
But you have plans

205
00:11:45,338 --> 00:11:48,035
on rebuilding the League
of Shadows? You've read

206
00:11:49,409 --> 00:11:51,378
the histories
that I left for you?

207
00:11:51,611 --> 00:11:54,445
I've read them. But I
need to do my own thing.

208
00:11:55,381 --> 00:11:57,350
Your "own thing"?

209
00:11:59,419 --> 00:12:00,682
With the power you gave me,

210
00:12:00,753 --> 00:12:04,190
I can rule Gotham like
no one ever has before.

211
00:12:04,457 --> 00:12:06,551
The people will
worship me like a queen.

212
00:12:07,794 --> 00:12:09,956
How disappointing.

213
00:12:11,998 --> 00:12:14,763
You're right. They should
worship me like a god.

214
00:12:14,867 --> 00:12:18,497
Enough. Give me your
hand so that I can take it back.

215
00:12:20,206 --> 00:12:23,370
No. It is mine. You promised me!

216
00:12:24,444 --> 00:12:27,209
I was mistaken in you, Barbara.

217
00:12:27,680 --> 00:12:28,943
"Mistaken"?

218
00:12:29,716 --> 00:12:30,911
Tell that to her.

219
00:12:32,685 --> 00:12:35,587
You think that is you.

220
00:12:37,624 --> 00:12:39,456
(RA'S LAUGHS)

221
00:12:40,893 --> 00:12:44,489
She was just a whore.

222
00:12:46,332 --> 00:12:49,734
I killed her out of pity.

223
00:12:50,737 --> 00:12:51,966
You're lying.

224
00:12:52,805 --> 00:12:55,172
The Demon's Head is my destiny.

225
00:12:55,275 --> 00:12:59,269
Then why have you
not unlocked its secrets?

226
00:12:59,946 --> 00:13:04,281
You sad, deluded woman.

227
00:13:05,418 --> 00:13:08,513
You thought you were
a reincarnated queen.

228
00:13:10,189 --> 00:13:15,890
But in truth, you're just an
unstable nightclub owner,

229
00:13:16,462 --> 00:13:20,797
<i>whose greatest accomplishment
was the murder of her own parents.</i>

230
00:13:21,801 --> 00:13:23,429
<i>You are nothing.</i>

231
00:13:25,405 --> 00:13:26,998
Now, give me your hand.

232
00:13:27,607 --> 00:13:31,942
Or I will kill you and take
The Demon's Head by force.

233
00:13:34,580 --> 00:13:36,105
Try it, zombie boy.

234
00:13:36,416 --> 00:13:37,975
(GRUNTING)

235
00:13:39,786 --> 00:13:40,947
(BARBARA GROANS)

236
00:13:43,122 --> 00:13:44,122
(NECK SNAPS)

237
00:13:55,868 --> 00:13:57,063
(GRUNTING)

238
00:13:57,337 --> 00:13:58,396
(BARBARA YELLING)

239
00:14:00,173 --> 00:14:01,732
Get her out of here. Go!

240
00:14:08,915 --> 00:14:10,008
(PANTING)

241
00:14:10,350 --> 00:14:11,350
I'm fine.

242
00:14:11,417 --> 00:14:12,417
(GRUNTS)

243
00:14:15,321 --> 00:14:16,687
(CAR SPEEDING)

244
00:14:16,789 --> 00:14:17,848
(TIRES SCREECHING)

245
00:14:19,158 --> 00:14:20,158
Get in!

246
00:14:22,495 --> 00:14:24,020
(ENGINE REVVING)

247
00:14:36,075 --> 00:14:37,873
MAN: All right,
you know the rules.

248
00:14:37,977 --> 00:14:39,912
Hands only, no drinking water.

249
00:14:40,012 --> 00:14:42,880
I want a good, clean
eat. Ready? Ready?

250
00:14:44,384 --> 00:14:46,353
- (CROWD CHEERING)
- (CHOMPING)

251
00:14:46,786 --> 00:14:48,414
- Come on, eat it.
- Come, come, come on.

252
00:14:50,590 --> 00:14:52,081
I'm looking for Lee Thompkins.

253
00:14:53,559 --> 00:14:54,583
The Doc.

254
00:14:58,264 --> 00:15:00,028
(CHEERING CONTINUES)

255
00:15:03,469 --> 00:15:04,469
Lee.

256
00:15:06,139 --> 00:15:07,139
(MAN VOMITING)

257
00:15:08,541 --> 00:15:09,541
The winner!

258
00:15:10,143 --> 00:15:13,204
Jim, you don't look like a
guy who got shot four times.

259
00:15:13,813 --> 00:15:15,373
Because you were
able to keep me alive.

260
00:15:16,382 --> 00:15:17,382
Thanks.

261
00:15:17,450 --> 00:15:19,050
I'd just shot Sofia
Falcone in the head.

262
00:15:19,085 --> 00:15:20,212
I was in a good mood.

263
00:15:22,755 --> 00:15:24,053
I'm looking for Ed Nygma.

264
00:15:25,258 --> 00:15:27,250
Five banks were
robbed last night.

265
00:15:27,360 --> 00:15:29,226
It has all the hallmarks
of a Nygma special.

266
00:15:30,096 --> 00:15:31,530
I haven't seen Ed in weeks.

267
00:15:33,766 --> 00:15:35,758
I know you feel
loyalty towards him,

268
00:15:36,068 --> 00:15:39,300
but you of all people should
know he's sick. He's a psychopath.

269
00:15:39,405 --> 00:15:40,634
We all have our flaws.

270
00:15:41,274 --> 00:15:42,469
(GORDON SIGHS)

271
00:15:42,875 --> 00:15:43,875
Lee.

272
00:15:45,244 --> 00:15:46,940
I can understand
why you're here,

273
00:15:47,480 --> 00:15:49,847
but there are other
ways of finding absolution.

274
00:15:50,750 --> 00:15:52,651
You can't take ownership
of everyone's problems.

275
00:15:52,819 --> 00:15:54,014
This is The Narrows.

276
00:15:54,120 --> 00:15:56,248
Nobody owns anything
down here but the slumlords.

277
00:15:57,457 --> 00:15:59,334
Why don't you try going
after the real criminals?

278
00:15:59,358 --> 00:16:01,327
The people making money
off the backs of the poor.

279
00:16:02,595 --> 00:16:04,530
You mean like Gotham
Savings and Loan?

280
00:16:06,766 --> 00:16:08,667
None of the guards were killed.

281
00:16:08,768 --> 00:16:12,034
The more I think about it,
doesn't exactly feel like Ed Nygma.

282
00:16:12,939 --> 00:16:15,101
- Or not just him.
- If we're done here...

283
00:16:19,445 --> 00:16:20,504
Whatever's happened,

284
00:16:21,647 --> 00:16:23,809
you can always
call me. I can help.

285
00:16:26,819 --> 00:16:28,310
You really don't
get it, do you, Jim?

286
00:16:30,523 --> 00:16:31,855
It's good to see you.

287
00:16:43,002 --> 00:16:44,698
Ra's just tried to kill
me because of you.

288
00:16:44,804 --> 00:16:46,582
You could have just given
him The Demon's Paw.

289
00:16:46,606 --> 00:16:47,665
"Head"!

290
00:16:47,874 --> 00:16:50,173
It's "The Demon's
Head" and it is mine!

291
00:16:50,710 --> 00:16:51,871
You betrayed me.

292
00:16:52,245 --> 00:16:54,077
I was trying to save
you from yourself.

293
00:16:54,714 --> 00:16:57,684
Also, the other day, you
actually told your thugs to kill me.

294
00:16:58,217 --> 00:16:59,480
It was a spanking.

295
00:16:59,685 --> 00:17:02,814
- If I wanted you dead, I would've...
- Oh, shut up, both of you!

296
00:17:03,322 --> 00:17:05,917
We're wasting time, Ra's
could be on his way right now.

297
00:17:06,025 --> 00:17:07,069
Which wouldn't be a problem

298
00:17:07,093 --> 00:17:08,337
if Barbara would just
give him what he wants.

299
00:17:08,361 --> 00:17:09,361
Never gonna happen.

300
00:17:09,428 --> 00:17:10,706
Okay, so what are
we gonna do, Barbara?

301
00:17:10,730 --> 00:17:12,875
We're just gonna walk around
with targets on our backs?

302
00:17:12,899 --> 00:17:14,993
No, we're gonna
kill the son of a bitch.

303
00:17:16,002 --> 00:17:17,163
The kid did it before, right?

304
00:17:17,603 --> 00:17:19,414
Yeah, but that was different.
We had, like, a special knife.

305
00:17:19,438 --> 00:17:21,532
Yeah, that one you got
from auction. Where is it?

306
00:17:21,607 --> 00:17:23,327
We gave it back to the
Nanda Parbat embassy.

307
00:17:23,376 --> 00:17:25,538
Great, so we'll just do
a little smash-and-grab

308
00:17:25,645 --> 00:17:26,855
and then I'll fillet the zombie.

309
00:17:26,879 --> 00:17:28,439
I have to be the
one holding the knife.

310
00:17:30,683 --> 00:17:33,653
It's part of the
ritual, like the blood.

311
00:17:35,588 --> 00:17:36,749
I have to kill him again.

312
00:17:39,025 --> 00:17:40,584
Even if that's the
case, Master Bruce,

313
00:17:40,693 --> 00:17:41,737
I can't allow you
to do it. Not again.

314
00:17:41,761 --> 00:17:43,389
We might not get
another chance, Alfred.

315
00:17:44,664 --> 00:17:45,825
This is the only way.

316
00:17:46,532 --> 00:17:48,694
Says you, the
mystical knife expert.

317
00:17:48,868 --> 00:17:52,270
I've got The Demon's Head. I
bet if I'm holding it in my hand...

318
00:17:54,073 --> 00:17:56,042
What if killing Ra's
unlocks my powers?

319
00:17:57,310 --> 00:17:59,454
Yeah, and what if you fail
and Ra's gets the knife back?

320
00:17:59,478 --> 00:18:00,789
We'll worry about
who kills him later.

321
00:18:00,813 --> 00:18:02,357
Right now, we have to get
the knife before Ra's does.

322
00:18:02,381 --> 00:18:05,101
TABITHA: Embassies are heavily
guarded. And we can't wait till night.

323
00:18:05,284 --> 00:18:07,879
We're gonna need guns, smoke
grenades to cause a diversion.

324
00:18:07,954 --> 00:18:09,946
If I may, there may
be another option.

325
00:18:11,657 --> 00:18:13,697
But you got to guarantee
not to stab us in the back.

326
00:18:14,994 --> 00:18:15,994
Again.

327
00:18:19,632 --> 00:18:22,625
So, in short, we'd like
to thank you very much.

328
00:18:22,735 --> 00:18:25,016
Both of us would like to thank
you for taking such good...

329
00:18:25,571 --> 00:18:26,698
Such good care of her.

330
00:18:27,273 --> 00:18:29,742
But now we'd like to take
the knife home. Please.

331
00:18:32,478 --> 00:18:35,141
It was never yours to
begin with, Mr. Pennyworth.

332
00:18:35,648 --> 00:18:37,549
It belongs to my people.

333
00:18:38,551 --> 00:18:41,077
When Mr. Bruce Wayne
purchased it at auction,

334
00:18:41,387 --> 00:18:44,414
he was rescuing a
looted historical treasure.

335
00:18:45,725 --> 00:18:48,058
That's why you
returned it to us.

336
00:18:48,628 --> 00:18:50,620
Yeah. But it was a
loan, wasn't it, mate?

337
00:18:52,231 --> 00:18:53,995
It was never meant as a keepsie.

338
00:18:55,301 --> 00:18:58,294
This knife is worth millions
and you just gave it away?

339
00:18:58,971 --> 00:19:01,634
- You idiot!
- Easy, muffin.

340
00:19:04,510 --> 00:19:07,639
Look, you look like you've got a
stable head on your shoulders.

341
00:19:08,014 --> 00:19:10,210
Why don't I make
a little donation,

342
00:19:10,950 --> 00:19:12,350
and you give us the knife,

343
00:19:13,519 --> 00:19:14,851
and we walk away?

344
00:19:14,987 --> 00:19:17,047
Does Bruce Wayne
even know about this?

345
00:19:18,691 --> 00:19:22,651
(SCOFFS) Whatever
your agenda is,

346
00:19:22,995 --> 00:19:26,193
I believe that you and
your chippie should leave.

347
00:19:27,166 --> 00:19:30,295
A chippie? Did you just
call my missus a chippie?

348
00:19:31,370 --> 00:19:33,805
What is that...

349
00:19:33,973 --> 00:19:36,340
What... A "chippie," is that
a new term or something...

350
00:19:36,976 --> 00:19:38,000
Something...

351
00:19:38,144 --> 00:19:39,203
(COUGHING)

352
00:19:39,311 --> 00:19:41,143
(STUTTERING) What?
What's happening?

353
00:19:41,347 --> 00:19:42,679
I can't breathe.

354
00:19:42,782 --> 00:19:44,526
Oh, my God. I think
he's having a heart attack.

355
00:19:44,550 --> 00:19:45,994
- I can't breathe.
- He's having a heart attack.

356
00:19:46,018 --> 00:19:47,018
(ALARM RINGING)

357
00:19:47,119 --> 00:19:49,111
- Look what you did.
- Tell the security

358
00:19:49,188 --> 00:19:50,315
it's a false alarm.

359
00:19:50,389 --> 00:19:51,933
I can't breathe. I can't
breathe. I can't breathe.

360
00:19:51,957 --> 00:19:53,802
Give me your jacket. Put
your jacket under his head.

361
00:19:53,826 --> 00:19:55,306
- Put your jacket.
- (ALFRED GROANING)

362
00:19:55,695 --> 00:19:58,290
It really hurts. It
really... It really hurts.

363
00:19:58,597 --> 00:19:59,597
(ALFRED GROANING)

364
00:20:02,535 --> 00:20:03,696
(ALFRED GROANING)

365
00:20:03,769 --> 00:20:05,738
TABITHA: All right,
you're gonna be just fine.

366
00:20:05,838 --> 00:20:07,101
It really hurts.

367
00:20:07,206 --> 00:20:08,206
(GRUNTS)

368
00:20:08,374 --> 00:20:09,374
Stay with me.

369
00:20:09,442 --> 00:20:10,933
Ooh, I feel much better now.

370
00:20:11,544 --> 00:20:13,206
(ALARM RINGING CONTINUES)

371
00:20:16,115 --> 00:20:18,050
Sorry about the fuss, fellas.

372
00:20:19,185 --> 00:20:20,209
"Chippie!"

373
00:20:25,391 --> 00:20:26,391
(DOOR OPENS)

374
00:20:26,625 --> 00:20:27,786
Oh!

375
00:20:36,235 --> 00:20:37,703
PENGUIN: <i>She's using you.</i>

376
00:20:38,204 --> 00:20:40,730
<i>Shame on you, stringing
along this troubled man.</i>

377
00:20:40,840 --> 00:20:42,365
(SIGHS) This troubled man.

378
00:20:43,576 --> 00:20:45,272
Oh, can't argue with that.

379
00:20:45,878 --> 00:20:47,278
Oh, no!

380
00:20:47,379 --> 00:20:50,008
Sorry. Just because you're in
charge, doesn't mean I disappear.

381
00:20:50,583 --> 00:20:53,712
That's because you're too
stupid to know when you've lost.

382
00:20:54,453 --> 00:20:57,719
Have I? "Lee, what am I to you?"

383
00:20:58,758 --> 00:21:00,056
Does that sound like you to you?

384
00:21:00,126 --> 00:21:02,789
Because to me,
that sounds like me.

385
00:21:04,096 --> 00:21:05,394
I'm not proud of that phrasing.

386
00:21:05,931 --> 00:21:08,298
I'm inside you,
buddy. Like a virus,

387
00:21:09,235 --> 00:21:10,498
infecting your thoughts.

388
00:21:10,603 --> 00:21:11,969
Oh, please.

389
00:21:12,138 --> 00:21:14,300
You couldn't even begin
to comprehend my thoughts,

390
00:21:14,406 --> 00:21:15,965
much less influence them.

391
00:21:16,142 --> 00:21:17,440
What about your feelings?

392
00:21:17,510 --> 00:21:18,808
How else would you explain

393
00:21:19,678 --> 00:21:21,670
those desperate attempts
to gain her approval?

394
00:21:22,414 --> 00:21:25,248
No. No, if anything,
she's the one who...

395
00:21:25,317 --> 00:21:27,411
You gave money away to the poor.

396
00:21:28,654 --> 00:21:31,180
- That was part of a larger plan.
- Yeah.

397
00:21:31,824 --> 00:21:33,824
Her plan. What did you
ever care about The Narrows?

398
00:21:33,926 --> 00:21:34,950
I don't.

399
00:21:35,327 --> 00:21:38,889
Every person here could
drown in a stew of their own filth,

400
00:21:38,964 --> 00:21:40,956
and I wouldn't
lose a wink of sleep.

401
00:21:41,066 --> 00:21:42,159
Oh, I know.

402
00:21:43,302 --> 00:21:46,431
Because all you
care about is her.

403
00:21:46,939 --> 00:21:49,568
(ECHOING) Just like I
did. So keep that up, buddy.

404
00:21:49,642 --> 00:21:54,103
'Cause soon, there will be no
telling where you end and I begin.

405
00:21:54,180 --> 00:21:55,239
(DOOR OPENS)

406
00:21:55,314 --> 00:21:56,314
(DOOR CREAKS)

407
00:21:56,582 --> 00:21:57,582
(DOOR CLOSES)

408
00:22:00,119 --> 00:22:01,348
That's not gonna happen.

409
00:22:08,360 --> 00:22:11,296
Well done. Now, knife, please.

410
00:22:13,299 --> 00:22:14,494
Selina, it has to be me.

411
00:22:16,202 --> 00:22:18,797
Selina, give me the knife.

412
00:22:19,572 --> 00:22:21,370
And you better scram
while you still can.

413
00:22:21,674 --> 00:22:22,835
I'm taking the knife!

414
00:22:23,075 --> 00:22:25,806
Oh, you do not want
to make me angry, kid.

415
00:22:25,878 --> 00:22:27,798
Sorry, "muffin", I'm gonna
need you to step back.

416
00:22:27,847 --> 00:22:30,874
Don't you even go there, love.
Selina, don't give her the knife.

417
00:22:31,517 --> 00:22:32,517
(SCOFFS) Screw this.

418
00:22:36,689 --> 00:22:38,817
Your arrogance is gonna
get someone killed, you know.

419
00:22:38,991 --> 00:22:40,892
- Or just you.
- Stop!

420
00:22:45,898 --> 00:22:46,898
Thank you.

421
00:22:47,867 --> 00:22:50,200
Now... Get in!

422
00:22:52,638 --> 00:22:53,833
Selina, let's go.

423
00:23:01,547 --> 00:23:02,742
(CAR DOOR CLOSES)

424
00:23:03,382 --> 00:23:04,406
(ENGINE STARTS)

425
00:23:05,551 --> 00:23:07,452
Nice doing business
with you, boys.

426
00:23:09,088 --> 00:23:10,249
(TIRES SCREECHING)

427
00:23:19,064 --> 00:23:20,088
You were right.

428
00:23:21,600 --> 00:23:22,727
She's using me.

429
00:23:23,702 --> 00:23:24,863
Finally.

430
00:23:25,304 --> 00:23:27,068
So much for you
being smart, now.

431
00:23:27,273 --> 00:23:29,435
Yeah. The most brilliant minds

432
00:23:29,541 --> 00:23:31,533
are often blind to the
most obvious truths.

433
00:23:32,077 --> 00:23:33,101
Finally.

434
00:23:34,046 --> 00:23:37,448
- And you came to me...
- Because that lovestruck moron, Ed,

435
00:23:37,950 --> 00:23:39,578
is floating down a
river of dopamine,

436
00:23:39,685 --> 00:23:42,086
deep within the primitive
reward circuit of my brain,

437
00:23:42,187 --> 00:23:44,088
and I need you to
help me drown him.

438
00:23:44,623 --> 00:23:45,623
For good.

439
00:23:46,292 --> 00:23:48,386
Did you bring the half-share
of profits we asked for?

440
00:23:48,694 --> 00:23:49,694
That money is gone.

441
00:23:50,229 --> 00:23:52,425
Distributed among the
riffraff of The Narrows. But...

442
00:23:54,934 --> 00:23:58,530
Those five banks were
merely the first stage

443
00:23:59,271 --> 00:24:00,762
of a very sophisticated plan.

444
00:24:01,740 --> 00:24:04,471
And the coup de
grâce is tonight.

445
00:24:05,210 --> 00:24:07,372
I knew you were
scheming something.

446
00:24:09,448 --> 00:24:11,474
That's why we were
gonna rob you afterward.

447
00:24:12,651 --> 00:24:14,347
But I prefer this way.

448
00:24:15,587 --> 00:24:17,579
There better be enough
in there to get me fixed.

449
00:24:18,257 --> 00:24:20,590
- Don't forget our deal.
- I won't.

450
00:24:20,759 --> 00:24:23,092
Thank you so much.
And how big is the score?

451
00:24:23,595 --> 00:24:24,961
About $100 million.

452
00:24:27,433 --> 00:24:28,433
Apiece.

453
00:24:33,706 --> 00:24:36,141
And you help me deal
with Lee Thompkins.

454
00:24:38,644 --> 00:24:39,644
(DOOR OPENS)

455
00:24:44,350 --> 00:24:45,682
Thank you for coming back.

456
00:24:46,618 --> 00:24:48,109
We serve The
Demon's Head, Barbara.

457
00:24:49,488 --> 00:24:50,488
So, what's the play?

458
00:24:51,023 --> 00:24:54,482
Simple. I do the flashlight
hand thingy, summon Ra's,

459
00:24:54,660 --> 00:24:57,687
little stabby-stab with the
knife, send him back to hell.

460
00:24:58,597 --> 00:24:59,637
Think I can remember that.

461
00:25:00,766 --> 00:25:01,927
<i>You can't be serious.</i>

462
00:25:02,468 --> 00:25:03,663
That's your plan?

463
00:25:04,269 --> 00:25:05,601
How do you expect
to get the drop

464
00:25:05,671 --> 00:25:08,505
on someone who's studied
kung fu for 2,000 years,

465
00:25:08,707 --> 00:25:09,707
and is a zombie?

466
00:25:09,808 --> 00:25:12,004
Not feeling a whole lot
of faith here, kitty-cat.

467
00:25:12,077 --> 00:25:14,656
Maybe I'd have a little more if you
knew how to use your demon head

468
00:25:14,680 --> 00:25:16,308
for something other
than a flashlight.

469
00:25:17,516 --> 00:25:18,711
You're gonna get us killed.

470
00:25:18,817 --> 00:25:20,057
You got any useful suggestions?

471
00:25:20,152 --> 00:25:22,018
- Maybe call backup.
- I did.

472
00:25:22,388 --> 00:25:24,880
- Here they are.
- What if Bruce is right?

473
00:25:25,157 --> 00:25:27,597
Let him use the knife. At least
we know that it worked before.

474
00:25:28,360 --> 00:25:29,851
You just took the
knife from him.

475
00:25:29,928 --> 00:25:31,396
Because you told
me to pick a side.

476
00:25:31,497 --> 00:25:33,398
I thought you had some
other plan other than

477
00:25:33,499 --> 00:25:36,025
"Let's stab the immortal undead
guy and hope for the best."

478
00:25:36,402 --> 00:25:38,997
Listen, Selina, we're
strongest when we're together.

479
00:25:40,005 --> 00:25:41,245
Now, are you in or are you out?

480
00:25:41,340 --> 00:25:43,172
If it's suicide
by Ra's, I'm out.

481
00:25:43,375 --> 00:25:44,502
Fine, then go.

482
00:25:54,186 --> 00:25:55,381
What if she's right?

483
00:25:56,822 --> 00:25:58,723
I can't control The
Demon's Head.

484
00:25:59,758 --> 00:26:01,590
Maybe it's like
Ra's said. Maybe...

485
00:26:02,528 --> 00:26:04,429
I am just a nightclub owner.

486
00:26:06,098 --> 00:26:07,657
I should have never
trusted those men.

487
00:26:09,868 --> 00:26:11,769
I didn't want you to
have The Demon's Head.

488
00:26:12,538 --> 00:26:14,063
Not even sure I want it now.

489
00:26:16,642 --> 00:26:18,907
Three years we've
been together, on and off.

490
00:26:20,813 --> 00:26:22,611
And I've never seen
you doubt yourself.

491
00:26:23,715 --> 00:26:25,775
So, however you
wanna play this, I'm in.

492
00:26:26,452 --> 00:26:28,045
But if you're saying
you're not worthy,

493
00:26:29,388 --> 00:26:30,788
that's where I jump ship.

494
00:26:34,326 --> 00:26:35,385
Let's do this.

495
00:26:55,581 --> 00:26:57,821
I suppose on the bright
side, you won't have to kill him.

496
00:26:58,584 --> 00:26:59,711
Again.

497
00:27:00,486 --> 00:27:03,081
- Except, I'm the only one who can.
- Well, so said Ra's.

498
00:27:04,623 --> 00:27:07,252
I mean, no disrespect to your
magical daggers and all of that,

499
00:27:07,326 --> 00:27:08,403
but I'd love to see
what would happen

500
00:27:08,427 --> 00:27:10,227
if I pulled his head off
his bloody shoulders.

501
00:27:11,630 --> 00:27:13,496
I can't believe Selina
gave Barbara the knife.

502
00:27:13,966 --> 00:27:14,966
(SCOFFS)

503
00:27:15,968 --> 00:27:18,528
Yeah, well, at least we
know where she stands.

504
00:27:18,971 --> 00:27:19,971
That's what you think.

505
00:27:23,108 --> 00:27:25,509
Oh, you got a bloody
cheek turning up here.

506
00:27:27,980 --> 00:27:31,144
I gave Barbara the knife
because if there was a chance

507
00:27:31,850 --> 00:27:33,546
she could use
it, I wanted her to.

508
00:27:33,886 --> 00:27:35,787
That way, Bruce
didn't have to kill him.

509
00:27:35,954 --> 00:27:37,274
I would've done
what I had to do.

510
00:27:37,523 --> 00:27:38,666
And you would've
gone straight back

511
00:27:38,690 --> 00:27:40,535
to being the douchebag
you've been the last few months.

512
00:27:40,559 --> 00:27:42,391
So, no, thank you.

513
00:27:42,728 --> 00:27:44,139
She's got a point
there, Master Bruce.

514
00:27:44,163 --> 00:27:46,155
Thanks for the explanation.
You can leave now.

515
00:27:46,498 --> 00:27:48,364
- Bruce...
- You sided with them.

516
00:27:49,868 --> 00:27:51,996
(SIGHS) Why does it
have to be about sides?

517
00:27:52,971 --> 00:27:54,098
There is somebody,

518
00:27:54,173 --> 00:27:56,267
something out there
that needs to be stopped.

519
00:27:56,341 --> 00:27:58,503
So why can't we focus on that?

520
00:27:59,811 --> 00:28:00,972
Another good point.

521
00:28:01,513 --> 00:28:03,880
Barbara and Tabitha are
gonna get themselves killed.

522
00:28:05,217 --> 00:28:06,708
And I don't want that to happen.

523
00:28:14,059 --> 00:28:15,619
GORDON: There
were easier banks to hit.

524
00:28:17,396 --> 00:28:19,695
- Why yours?
- I keep telling you.

525
00:28:20,165 --> 00:28:21,497
I have no idea.

526
00:28:22,768 --> 00:28:24,768
I'm the victim. You're
treating me like a criminal.

527
00:28:25,070 --> 00:28:26,663
Yeah, I wonder where
we'd get that from.

528
00:28:27,673 --> 00:28:29,869
- Excuse me?
- We did some digging,

529
00:28:30,075 --> 00:28:33,239
and your bank has been
investigated for redlining,

530
00:28:33,345 --> 00:28:35,109
usury, illegal foreclosures.

531
00:28:35,214 --> 00:28:36,682
And cleared on all counts.

532
00:28:37,616 --> 00:28:38,616
You have good lawyers.

533
00:28:39,384 --> 00:28:40,784
So we deserve to be robbed?

534
00:28:42,955 --> 00:28:43,955
I'm done here.

535
00:28:44,056 --> 00:28:46,855
Ma'am, can you just
give us a second, please?

536
00:28:49,261 --> 00:28:50,261
(DOOR OPENS)

537
00:28:53,565 --> 00:28:55,557
- What the hell are you doing?
- She's a crook.

538
00:28:55,667 --> 00:28:57,045
A bigger crook than
whoever ripped her off.

539
00:28:57,069 --> 00:28:58,069
You mean like Lee?

540
00:28:58,403 --> 00:28:59,981
Look, brother, I know
what this is about.

541
00:29:00,005 --> 00:29:02,907
You went down to The Narrows
and came back all fired up, okay?

542
00:29:03,008 --> 00:29:05,273
But alienating her
is not gonna help us.

543
00:29:05,877 --> 00:29:07,402
If Lee's involved with Nygma,

544
00:29:07,512 --> 00:29:09,572
we got to stop it
before it goes bad.

545
00:29:14,953 --> 00:29:16,854
Which of your branches
are the most vulnerable?

546
00:29:17,189 --> 00:29:19,090
As of this afternoon,
none of them.

547
00:29:19,258 --> 00:29:21,159
We have a security protocol.

548
00:29:21,460 --> 00:29:23,656
After the Arkham breakout
and the robberies...

549
00:29:23,762 --> 00:29:25,594
You moved your assets
to a secure location.

550
00:29:25,664 --> 00:29:26,723
Yes, of course.

551
00:29:26,798 --> 00:29:29,131
All 45 branches, this morning.

552
00:29:30,335 --> 00:29:34,238
It's totally safe. Fortified
and heavily guarded.

553
00:29:34,473 --> 00:29:35,473
Where is it?

554
00:29:44,249 --> 00:29:46,684
- Pistol would've been more fun.
- You indulge me.

555
00:29:46,985 --> 00:29:48,977
Breaking open the
vault is the last detail.

556
00:29:49,154 --> 00:29:50,952
Big detail. How
did you solve it?

557
00:29:51,123 --> 00:29:52,591
A little help from some friends.

558
00:29:55,227 --> 00:29:57,423
I'm the revealer of masks.

559
00:29:58,096 --> 00:29:59,257
When I appear,

560
00:30:00,065 --> 00:30:02,091
friend becomes foe,

561
00:30:02,601 --> 00:30:03,641
and the one that you love,

562
00:30:04,970 --> 00:30:07,166
becomes the one that
you hate. What am I?

563
00:30:08,073 --> 00:30:09,073
Betrayal.

564
00:30:10,442 --> 00:30:11,603
Hello, Lee.

565
00:30:11,810 --> 00:30:12,810
(GASPS)

566
00:30:13,779 --> 00:30:16,408
Yeah, it's not a
dart gun. Let's go.

567
00:30:27,793 --> 00:30:28,988
(SWORD SWISHING)

568
00:30:47,179 --> 00:30:48,179
(ELECTRICITY BUZZING)

569
00:30:50,382 --> 00:30:51,406
(BREATHES HEAVILY)

570
00:30:53,051 --> 00:30:55,816
- Nice entrance.
- I do hope you've reconsidered,

571
00:30:56,621 --> 00:30:59,113
and are planning to
give me what I want.

572
00:30:59,725 --> 00:31:01,694
I've thought about it. A lot.

573
00:31:02,327 --> 00:31:03,488
And about us.

574
00:31:04,696 --> 00:31:06,187
We had something, didn't we?

575
00:31:07,399 --> 00:31:09,630
Back when you
were less dug up-y.

576
00:31:10,001 --> 00:31:12,232
I do not have time for this.

577
00:31:12,337 --> 00:31:13,805
I will give you what
you want, Ra's.

578
00:31:15,140 --> 00:31:17,871
But I want you to admit
we had a connection.

579
00:31:18,643 --> 00:31:20,339
And that those
things you said to me

580
00:31:20,412 --> 00:31:22,711
were just mind games to
make me lose my nerve.

581
00:31:23,548 --> 00:31:26,780
You want me to tell
you that you're special?

582
00:31:27,552 --> 00:31:28,713
Would that be so hard?

583
00:31:29,921 --> 00:31:30,921
No.

584
00:31:32,257 --> 00:31:33,418
And moreover,

585
00:31:34,059 --> 00:31:37,120
it's true. You are special.

586
00:31:38,296 --> 00:31:41,061
I'm just sorry it had to
come to this, Barbara.

587
00:31:44,102 --> 00:31:45,102
Me, too.

588
00:31:46,738 --> 00:31:47,938
But thank you for saying that.

589
00:31:51,943 --> 00:31:52,943
(GASPS)

590
00:31:54,079 --> 00:31:55,274
Ouch.

591
00:31:58,517 --> 00:31:59,517
(GASPS)

592
00:31:59,584 --> 00:32:00,779
She must do this by herself.

593
00:32:02,621 --> 00:32:03,621
(BARBARA SCREAMS)

594
00:32:04,189 --> 00:32:05,555
(GRUNTING)

595
00:32:11,430 --> 00:32:12,625
(BARBARA CHOKING)

596
00:32:14,466 --> 00:32:15,593
(STRAINING)

597
00:32:18,270 --> 00:32:19,270
Barbara, fight.

598
00:32:25,410 --> 00:32:26,410
(GRUNTS)

599
00:32:27,412 --> 00:32:29,074
But this is Barbara's fight.

600
00:32:29,948 --> 00:32:30,948
(PANTING)

601
00:32:36,588 --> 00:32:37,783
(GASPING)

602
00:32:56,141 --> 00:32:57,666
But this is Barbara's fight.

603
00:33:02,147 --> 00:33:04,844
Well, now. Look at you.

604
00:33:04,950 --> 00:33:05,950
Yeah. Look at me.

605
00:33:06,985 --> 00:33:08,476
You wanna give it another shot?

606
00:33:12,324 --> 00:33:13,324
(GRUNTS)

607
00:33:16,495 --> 00:33:18,088
She's mastered The Demon's Head.

608
00:33:18,463 --> 00:33:19,522
Wow!

609
00:33:19,764 --> 00:33:21,528
I can see why
he likes this thing.

610
00:33:22,934 --> 00:33:24,197
That's enough.

611
00:33:24,936 --> 00:33:28,600
Give me what I want
or your friend dies.

612
00:33:29,207 --> 00:33:31,005
I thought this was between us.

613
00:33:31,209 --> 00:33:33,075
Choose now.

614
00:33:38,884 --> 00:33:40,250
Tabby, I...

615
00:33:42,387 --> 00:33:43,753
I can't give this up.

616
00:33:44,489 --> 00:33:45,513
(GASPS)

617
00:33:56,501 --> 00:33:57,560
No!

618
00:34:03,174 --> 00:34:04,574
That's enough.

619
00:34:05,176 --> 00:34:07,702
Choose now.

620
00:34:13,218 --> 00:34:14,218
You win.

621
00:34:17,022 --> 00:34:18,022
Just don't hurt her.

622
00:34:21,159 --> 00:34:22,159
(PANTS)

623
00:34:26,197 --> 00:34:27,597
Barbara Kean,

624
00:34:28,066 --> 00:34:30,160
you surprise me yet again.

625
00:34:31,136 --> 00:34:34,072
Maybe I wasn't
mistaken in you after all.

626
00:34:57,495 --> 00:34:59,828
(RA'S GRUNTING)

627
00:35:07,105 --> 00:35:08,733
(EXHALES HEAVILY)

628
00:35:17,282 --> 00:35:18,282
Give me the knife, Ra's.

629
00:35:19,718 --> 00:35:20,742
Let me kill you.

630
00:35:26,291 --> 00:35:28,089
Today is not the day that I die.

631
00:35:51,483 --> 00:35:53,723
NYGMA: This is the price for
taking advantage of me, Lee.

632
00:35:53,885 --> 00:35:55,820
You're wrong, Ed.
I wasn't using you.

633
00:35:55,887 --> 00:35:57,515
Again, don't call me "Ed."

634
00:35:58,356 --> 00:35:59,619
And I'm not wrong about you.

635
00:36:00,492 --> 00:36:02,290
Truck is almost
full. We should go.

636
00:36:02,494 --> 00:36:04,414
Tell the ogre, have him
leave the property deeds.

637
00:36:04,496 --> 00:36:06,522
They all belong to The
Narrows. Worthless.

638
00:36:07,999 --> 00:36:08,999
(CHUCKLES)

639
00:36:09,100 --> 00:36:11,968
And so ends the tale of
the Queen of The Narrows.

640
00:36:12,370 --> 00:36:13,370
Hmm?

641
00:36:13,505 --> 00:36:16,134
Goodbye, Lee. (LAUGHING)

642
00:36:19,644 --> 00:36:20,644
What are you doing?

643
00:36:20,712 --> 00:36:21,941
How did that go again?

644
00:36:22,213 --> 00:36:27,277
"And the revealer of masks,
when I appear, friend becomes foe."

645
00:36:28,119 --> 00:36:29,678
- Betrayal.
- Exactly.

646
00:36:32,824 --> 00:36:34,122
(ALARM RINGING)

647
00:36:38,830 --> 00:36:39,874
What the hell are you doing?

648
00:36:39,898 --> 00:36:41,242
Just burning The
Narrows' property deeds.

649
00:36:41,266 --> 00:36:42,427
Not that.

650
00:36:42,534 --> 00:36:45,003
He's proving his
love by betraying us.

651
00:36:46,104 --> 00:36:47,715
These bars can't hold
me. When I get out...

652
00:36:47,739 --> 00:36:48,739
We'll be gone.

653
00:36:49,507 --> 00:36:51,032
I just wanted you
to hear something.

654
00:36:53,211 --> 00:36:54,851
Oswald, we've been
through thick and thin.

655
00:36:55,747 --> 00:36:57,841
And I hold no grudge on you.

656
00:36:59,684 --> 00:37:01,346
But you come against Lee,

657
00:37:02,020 --> 00:37:03,249
and you come against me.

658
00:37:04,923 --> 00:37:07,324
I'm gonna dismember
you, you twerp!

659
00:37:07,559 --> 00:37:08,993
Yep, not even
gonna try with you.

660
00:37:10,028 --> 00:37:11,394
Let's go, Lee.

661
00:37:11,563 --> 00:37:13,031
It won't make any difference.

662
00:37:13,998 --> 00:37:15,432
She's still using you.

663
00:37:15,834 --> 00:37:19,236
You are not the
Riddler, you are a fool!

664
00:37:19,437 --> 00:37:20,769
God...

665
00:37:21,005 --> 00:37:22,234
(STRAINING)

666
00:37:25,610 --> 00:37:26,610
Why do that?

667
00:37:26,711 --> 00:37:29,772
Why bring Penguin and Grundy if
you're just gonna lock them inside?

668
00:37:29,881 --> 00:37:31,372
I needed Grundy
to open the vault.

669
00:37:31,549 --> 00:37:33,108
And Oswald was
gonna rob us anyway,

670
00:37:33,218 --> 00:37:34,447
so, just kept an eye on him.

671
00:37:34,719 --> 00:37:36,347
He'll get over it, or he won't.

672
00:37:36,421 --> 00:37:37,912
So you don't think
I'm using you?

673
00:37:39,157 --> 00:37:40,819
No, I know you are.

674
00:37:41,593 --> 00:37:43,459
Then why would you
betray your friends for me?

675
00:37:44,963 --> 00:37:45,963
Is this...

676
00:37:46,664 --> 00:37:48,565
- Are you Ed?
- No, I'm me.

677
00:37:49,768 --> 00:37:52,294
- How can you be sure?
- Because Ed didn't understand you.

678
00:37:53,738 --> 00:37:56,572
He didn't see how deeply
you had changed. I do.

679
00:37:57,609 --> 00:37:58,975
I know that that virus

680
00:37:59,978 --> 00:38:01,913
woke up something
deep inside you.

681
00:38:03,248 --> 00:38:05,649
And you let that something
loose when you shot Sofia.

682
00:38:06,785 --> 00:38:08,583
And you love it.

683
00:38:10,455 --> 00:38:11,582
And I love it, too.

684
00:38:12,123 --> 00:38:14,043
And I know that you don't
feel same way about me.

685
00:38:17,729 --> 00:38:18,788
But you will.

686
00:38:19,964 --> 00:38:21,933
And when you do, I will be here.

687
00:38:25,804 --> 00:38:26,999
Ed Nygma,

688
00:38:27,806 --> 00:38:29,172
you are a riddle.

689
00:38:31,276 --> 00:38:33,108
That's the nicest thing
someone's said to me.

690
00:38:33,311 --> 00:38:34,904
(SIRENS WAILING)

691
00:38:35,914 --> 00:38:37,974
- That's Jim.
- This alarm just went off.

692
00:38:38,082 --> 00:38:39,414
He was on to us.

693
00:38:40,018 --> 00:38:42,338
- We can just go out the back.
- No, they'll see the truck.

694
00:38:42,620 --> 00:38:44,145
One of us needs
to distract them.

695
00:38:46,191 --> 00:38:47,215
Done.

696
00:38:47,892 --> 00:38:48,892
No!

697
00:38:50,028 --> 00:38:51,394
I can handle Jim Gordon.

698
00:38:52,030 --> 00:38:53,555
You take the money
to The Narrows.

699
00:38:55,366 --> 00:38:58,029
- You trust me?
- I do.

700
00:39:02,507 --> 00:39:03,507
Go.

701
00:39:14,052 --> 00:39:17,022
GORDON: <i>GCPD. Nygma,
we know you're in there.</i>

702
00:39:17,121 --> 00:39:18,384
<i>Come out with your hands up.</i>

703
00:39:24,362 --> 00:39:25,362
(DOOR CLOSES)

704
00:39:26,231 --> 00:39:27,995
Sweet merciful mother.

705
00:39:37,041 --> 00:39:38,304
You know your rights.

706
00:40:18,716 --> 00:40:19,740
(SIGHS)

707
00:40:30,628 --> 00:40:31,926
You'd have done the same for me.

708
00:40:46,244 --> 00:40:48,839
Ladies, I hope this
isn't one of those

709
00:40:48,947 --> 00:40:51,075
"kill the old queen" situations.

710
00:40:51,683 --> 00:40:52,844
We discussed things.

711
00:40:53,084 --> 00:40:55,781
Demon's Head or not, you fought.

712
00:40:56,421 --> 00:40:58,583
Not for yourself, but
those alongside you.

713
00:41:00,625 --> 00:41:02,685
You are worthy, Barbara Kean.

714
00:41:08,700 --> 00:41:11,192
We follow you to our
deaths and beyond.

715
00:41:21,612 --> 00:41:23,924
We can find from Barbara where the
League hides temples, safe houses.

716
00:41:23,948 --> 00:41:25,143
He'll be in one of them.

717
00:41:25,249 --> 00:41:26,740
Meanwhile, we'll
try to fix the knife.

718
00:41:26,818 --> 00:41:29,218
Yeah, we'll just take it to the
magic knife shop, no problem.

719
00:41:29,821 --> 00:41:31,756
- Selina, be serious.
- I am.

720
00:41:32,090 --> 00:41:34,150
If Ra's wanted you
dead, you would be.

721
00:41:34,525 --> 00:41:35,925
He obviously likes you.

722
00:41:36,594 --> 00:41:38,586
- It's not about me.
- I know it's not about you.

723
00:41:39,097 --> 00:41:40,121
(SELINA SIGHS)

724
00:41:40,965 --> 00:41:43,127
Gotham has managed
a long time without you.

725
00:41:44,702 --> 00:41:47,831
It can manage a little longer,
if you have one night off.

726
00:41:50,908 --> 00:41:52,001
(SIGHS)

727
00:41:53,711 --> 00:41:54,906
You did good today.

728
00:41:59,050 --> 00:42:00,177
So did you.

729
00:42:01,419 --> 00:42:02,419
RA'S: Ahem.

730
00:42:02,854 --> 00:42:04,982
Poor timing. Apologies.

731
00:42:05,656 --> 00:42:09,491
I only want to
talk. Alone, please.

732
00:42:10,428 --> 00:42:11,428
I'm staying.

733
00:42:13,431 --> 00:42:14,592
Very well.

734
00:42:15,533 --> 00:42:16,728
She's right, you know, Bruce.

735
00:42:17,869 --> 00:42:18,996
I do like you.

736
00:42:19,137 --> 00:42:21,017
Respect you. Respect
you for what you'll become.

737
00:42:25,009 --> 00:42:27,137
You have no idea
what I'll become.

738
00:42:27,345 --> 00:42:28,574
Of course, I do.

739
00:42:29,013 --> 00:42:31,573
At least, who you could become.

740
00:42:33,518 --> 00:42:36,511
- Why are you here?
- I felt I owed you an explanation

741
00:42:37,188 --> 00:42:38,986
as to why I chose to live.

742
00:42:39,757 --> 00:42:41,385
When I took back
The Demon's Head,

743
00:42:41,492 --> 00:42:44,587
I saw a vision

744
00:42:46,564 --> 00:42:49,693
of a cataclysmic event
soon to befall this city.

745
00:42:51,369 --> 00:42:52,369
What event?

746
00:42:53,204 --> 00:42:57,073
A cleansing fire
that will destroy,

747
00:42:57,875 --> 00:42:59,207
purify,

748
00:43:00,044 --> 00:43:01,979
create. Create you, Bruce.

749
00:43:03,214 --> 00:43:05,945
Because I will use
it as a mighty forge,

750
00:43:06,084 --> 00:43:10,249
molding you into a
dark knight of Gotham.

751
00:43:13,124 --> 00:43:14,615
(SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING)

752
00:43:19,130 --> 00:43:20,758
If it doesn't kill you, that is.

753
00:44:02,473 --> 00:44:03,473
English - SDH
